Integer 0-100; default 100. Controls the whole-show proven-corruption threshold. All-proven-corrupt shows are still trashed regardless of the setting, while unverifiable corruption checks fail closed and do not trigger Trash or mutation work.}\cell\row\pard \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
Acceptable corruption % controls when proven corruption removes the entire logical show. The value is 0-100 and defaults to 100; the whole-show threshold is exceeded only when proven_corrupt * 100 is greater than acceptable_percent * total_audio, so equality is allowed. If every audio file in the logical show is proven corrupt, the logical show is sent to Trash/Recycle Bin regardless of this setting. When the logical show remains, a physical music folder whose directly contained audio is all proven corrupt is sent to Trash/Recycle Bin when it can be removed without taking healthy nested music with it, and other proven-corrupt audio files are trashed individually before later mutation work. A file that cannot be verified because of permission, I/O, unavailable-volume, timeout/resource, or validator-infrastructure failure is not automatically treated as corrupt. If corruption verification for a show is incomplete, TLO fails closed: it performs no corruption Trash action and skips rename, tag, Copy/Delete, and SHN-conversion mutations for that show while still allowing inventory metadata to be recorded. TLO never permanently deletes as a Trash fallback. Dry run reports WOULD_REMOVE/WOULD_NOT_TRASH-style planned results without changing anything.}
